</nav></div></header><main><section class="zk-hero"><div class="zk-wrap"><div class="zk-eyebrow">PRIVACY &amp; GDPR</div><h1>Website Privacy Notice.</h1><p>How ZKTeco WFM handles personal information associated with this website and the privacy choices that may apply.</p></div></section><section class="zk-section"><div class="zk-wrap"><div class="zk-notice"><strong>Important:</strong> This website privacy notice is a launch-ready draft intended for review by ZKTeco WFM legal/privacy counsel before production publication. It should be updated whenever website forms, analytics, advertising, CRM, chat or other data-processing technologies change.</div><div class="zk-legal-copy"><h2>1. Scope</h2><p>This notice describes how ZKTeco WFM may collect and use personal information through this website and related website interactions. Product/service data processing may be governed by separate customer agreements, product documentation, privacy policies or notices.</p><h2>2. Information We May Collect</h2><ul><li>Contact and professional information you provide, such as name, company, role, email, phone number and message content.</li><li>Support, sales or resource-request information you choose to submit.</li><li>Technical information such as browser type, device information, IP address, referring page and website activity when applicable technologies are enabled.</li><li>Cookie and privacy-preference information.</li></ul><h2>3. How We Use Information</h2><ul><li>Respond to inquiries and provide requested information.</li><li>Support customers and partners.</li><li>Operate, secure and improve the website.</li><li>Manage business relationships and communications.</li><li>Meet legal, regulatory and contractual obligations.</li><li>Conduct marketing where permitted and subject to applicable choices or consent.</li></ul><h2>4. Legal Bases for EEA/UK Processing</h2><p>Where GDPR or UK GDPR applies, processing may be based on consent, contractual necessity, compliance with legal obligations, legitimate interests, or another lawful basis appropriate to the activity. Consent can be withdrawn where processing relies on consent.</p><h2>5. Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2><p>Necessary technologies support core site functions. Optional analytics or marketing technologies should not be activated for visitors who require consent until an appropriate choice has been obtained. See the <a href="cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a> and use <button data-cookie-settings="" style="border:0;background:none;color:#201f62;font-weight:800;cursor:pointer;padding:0">Cookie Preferences</button> to manage choices.</p><h2>6. Sharing and Service Providers</h2><p>Information may be shared with service providers, affiliates, advisers or authorities when appropriate to operate the website, respond to requests, support business operations, protect rights and security, or comply with law. Service providers should receive only the information reasonably necessary for their role and be subject to appropriate safeguards.</p><h2>7. International Data Transfers</h2><p>Information may be processed in countries different from where it was collected. Where required, ZKTeco uses appropriate transfer mechanisms and safeguards. ZKTeco also maintains a separate Data Privacy Framework policy addressing applicable EU, UK and Swiss transfers.</p><h2>8. Retention</h2><p>Personal information is retained for as long as reasonably necessary for the purpose for which it was collected, to maintain business records, resolve disputes, protect security and meet applicable legal or contractual requirements.</p><h2>9. Your Privacy Rights</h2><p>Depending on location and applicable law, individuals may have rights to request access, correction, deletion, restriction, portability, objection, withdrawal of consent, or information about certain disclosures or sharing. Rights are subject to legal limitations and verification requirements.</p><h2>10. U.S. State Privacy Rights</h2><p>Residents of certain U.S. states may have additional rights under applicable state privacy laws. ZKTeco WFM will evaluate verified requests under the law applicable to the individual and the relevant processing activity.</p><h2>11. Biometric Information</h2><p>This website notice does not replace product- or service-specific biometric privacy obligations. Review the current <a href="https://zktecowfm.com/biometric-privacy-policy/">ZKTeco WFM Biometric Privacy Policy</a> where applicable.</p><h2>12. Security</h2><p>ZKTeco WFM uses administrative, technical and organizational measures intended to protect information appropriate to the nature of the processing. No security program or method of transmission can guarantee absolute security.</p><h2>13. Children</h2><p>This website is intended for business audiences and is not directed to children.</p><h2>14. Contact and Requests</h2><p>Privacy questions and requests can be submitted through our <a href="contact">Contact page</a>. Additional privacy information is available through the <a href="security-trust">Security &amp; Trust</a> area and existing ZKTeco privacy policies.</p><h2>15. Changes</h2><p>We may update this notice to reflect changes in our website, technologies, business practices or legal requirements. The current version should display the latest effective date when published.</p></div></div></section></main><footer class="zk-global-footer"><div class="zk-footer-shell"><div class="zk-footer-grid"><div class="zk-footer-brand"><img alt="ZKTeco WFM" class="zk-footer-logo" src="/assets/ZKTecowfm-white-green@4x.png" width="180"/><p>The Workforce Data Collection Company.<br/>Every Punch Matters.</p></div><div class="zk-footer-col"><h4>Solutions</h4><a href="workday">Workday Customers</a><a href="software-partners">Software Partners</a><a href="use-cases">Industry Use Cases</a><a href="customer-stories">Customer Stories</a></div><div class="zk-footer-col"><h4>Products</h4><a href="ultima-series">Ultima Series</a><a href="timetrack"